324
00:55:35,288 --> 00:55:36,028
[SPEAKER_02]: So you guys remember

325
00:55:39,040 --> 00:55:43,341
[SPEAKER_02]: There was this terrible storm that blew through in January.

326
00:55:44,261 --> 00:55:46,641
[SPEAKER_02]: I was in New Orleans for Folk Alliance.

327
00:55:48,222 --> 00:55:51,182
[SPEAKER_02]: And I almost got stuck.

328
00:55:51,222 --> 00:55:52,242
[SPEAKER_02]: A bunch of people almost got stuck.

329
00:55:52,262 --> 00:55:55,043
[SPEAKER_02]: And it was that storm that shut the whole Northeast down for three days.

330
00:55:55,083 --> 00:55:57,323
[SPEAKER_02]: And then it went through all of the South.

331
00:55:57,403 --> 00:55:58,924
[SPEAKER_02]: And Nashville froze over.

332
00:55:59,024 --> 00:56:01,044
[SPEAKER_02]: And a bunch of people lost their power for a couple weeks.

333
00:56:01,104 --> 00:56:02,184
[SPEAKER_02]: And it was a big mess.

334
00:56:02,224 --> 00:56:05,125
[SPEAKER_02]: And I was thinking about Leahy.

335
00:56:06,285 --> 00:56:12,787
[SPEAKER_02]: potentially getting snowed in in your new home and like all of all of this stuff and just thinking about all the people who are trying to get home to their loved ones.

336
00:56:13,548 --> 00:56:15,228
[SPEAKER_02]: And so I wrote this song, Caught in a Storm.

337
00:56:16,209 --> 00:56:26,432
[SPEAKER_02]: And so it's about being caught in a storm with wanting to be caught in a storm with the people that you love, both literally and metaphorically.

338
00:56:26,472 --> 00:56:26,713
[SPEAKER_02]: Thank you.

339
00:56:26,733 --> 00:56:27,613
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the word I was looking for.

