[SPEAKER_08]: Will the angel on my shoulder ever take the demons down?

374
01:02:48,318 --> 01:02:54,980
[SPEAKER_08]: Will I be so discontent with each curve in the road?

375
01:02:55,980 --> 01:03:02,782
[SPEAKER_08]: Will I have some gratefulness and learn to stand on that alone?

376
01:03:03,602 --> 01:03:10,024
[SPEAKER_08]: Can I be more in control of the thoughts that bring me down?

377
01:03:11,911 --> 01:03:18,218
[SPEAKER_08]: Will the angel on my shoulder ever take the demons down?

378
01:03:35,688 --> 01:03:42,872
[SPEAKER_08]: Everything I know I'll ask myself when I'm older and gray.

379
01:03:43,513 --> 01:03:46,835
[SPEAKER_08]: Will I wish I'd said goodbye?

380
01:03:47,635 --> 01:03:50,437
[SPEAKER_08]: Will I be so glad I stayed?

381
01:03:51,037 --> 01:03:57,722
[SPEAKER_08]: I think that I'll be glad I stayed when I lie where flowers lay.

382
01:03:59,707 --> 01:04:06,650
[SPEAKER_08]: Can I be more in control of the thoughts that bring me down?

383
01:04:08,410 --> 01:04:15,813
[SPEAKER_08]: Will the angel on my shoulder ever take the demons down?

384
01:04:19,754 --> 01:04:20,015
[SPEAKER_02]: Thank you.

385
01:04:20,055 --> 01:04:20,435
[SPEAKER_02]: Thank you.

386
01:04:20,775 --> 01:04:21,135
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm Parai.

387
01:04:34,162 --> 01:04:38,163
[SPEAKER_01]: So, wow.

388
01:04:38,583 --> 01:04:48,486
[SPEAKER_01]: So what we're trying to do here is we're trying to establish a tradition now of having at least one big voice every time we come out and do the Jazz Festival.

389
01:04:48,866 --> 01:04:52,547
[SPEAKER_01]: So last year we had Donna McElroy, and y'all know what that was.

390
01:04:53,227 --> 01:04:56,728
[SPEAKER_01]: And this year it's Farahi Malik, and it was just huge.

391
01:04:56,849 --> 01:04:58,889
[SPEAKER_01]: So thank you so much.

392
01:04:59,569 --> 01:05:00,730
[SPEAKER_01]: Thank you so much.

393
01:05:04,955 --> 01:05:24,640
[SPEAKER_01]: Once again, the Farai Malik Quintet, Farai Malik on vocals and acoustic guitar, Grayson Hillen on electric guitar, Jacob Means on vocals and meandering, Max Ridley back here on vocals in the upright bass, and Hector Falu Guzman on the traps back here.

394
01:05:25,121 --> 01:05:26,481
[SPEAKER_01]: Marvelous, just marvelous.

395
01:05:35,462 --> 01:05:39,363
[SPEAKER_01]: No worries, so we're gonna need to take a little pause for the cars to switch over groups.

396
01:05:40,584 --> 01:05:49,727
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'll be back with you in a little while, but in the meantime, please go inside and check out the offerings of the Danish Pastry House.

397
01:05:50,047 --> 01:05:52,688
[SPEAKER_01]: They have some real deliciousness there.

398
01:05:52,728 --> 01:05:56,430
[SPEAKER_01]: They've got savory, they've got sweet, so please go check them out.

399
01:05:56,810 --> 01:05:59,571
[SPEAKER_01]: Check out the t-shirts upstairs on the deck.

400
01:05:59,991 --> 01:06:05,957
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, that mint green and that bright orange, right, will set your wardrobe off for the next month.

401
01:06:06,698 --> 01:06:09,601
[SPEAKER_01]: So you need to have one of those in your collection.

402
01:06:10,682 --> 01:06:13,405
[SPEAKER_01]: So we're free, but we're not cheap.

403
01:06:13,925 --> 01:06:17,489
[SPEAKER_01]: So make sure that you make a donation to the cause.

404
01:06:17,629 --> 01:06:23,435
[SPEAKER_01]: See Shayla, she's got the red box, you know, drop a little coin or a little folding money, preferably folding money.

405
01:06:24,335 --> 01:06:26,817
[SPEAKER_01]: in there, and we're happy to have you here.

406
01:06:26,857 --> 01:06:37,345
[SPEAKER_01]: We hope you're enjoying yourselves, and we will be back very shortly with Mina Cho and her group, so get ready for something additionally special.

