460
01:32:43,032 --> 01:32:51,921
[SPEAKER_01]: So I mentioned when I was introducing Farai and her group that we met at Somerville Community Baptist Church.

461
01:32:52,982 --> 01:32:58,187
[SPEAKER_01]: Stacey Clayton, who's a great singer, who's been in this area for years and years,

462
01:32:59,027 --> 01:33:08,949
[SPEAKER_01]: She does an annual concert with Pastor David and Mina and folks over at Somerville Community Baptist.

463
01:33:09,089 --> 01:33:16,890
[SPEAKER_01]: And I've been lucky enough, fortunate enough, for them to bring me on board to do poetry and to emcee.

464
01:33:17,070 --> 01:33:24,611
[SPEAKER_01]: And I met Farai, and I also met Mina, who is the director of music at the church.

465
01:33:25,132 --> 01:33:27,212
[SPEAKER_01]: But she's much more than that.

466
01:33:30,094 --> 01:33:44,521
[SPEAKER_01]: The Minichuk Cho Quartet brings the bold, joyful sound of gugak jazz, where Korea's century-old rhythms, felt melodies, and ritual traditions meet the improvisational fire of modern jazz.

467
01:33:44,561 --> 01:33:46,942
[SPEAKER_01]: So prepare for something very, very different.

468
01:33:47,764 --> 01:33:50,946
[SPEAKER_01]: led by pianist and composer Dr. Mina Cho.

469
01:33:52,808 --> 01:33:58,452
[SPEAKER_01]: And I actually like to call her double doctor because she actually has two doctorates.

470
01:33:59,733 --> 01:34:02,134
[SPEAKER_01]: One from Brenda?

471
01:34:03,315 --> 01:34:08,880
[SPEAKER_01]: New England Conservatory, and one from Brandeis.

472
01:34:09,301 --> 01:34:17,948
[SPEAKER_01]: And she's a Boston-based jazz pianist, composer, and really, really a scholar in all areas of musicology and so forth.

473
01:34:18,929 --> 01:34:24,694
[SPEAKER_01]: So you're in for not only an education, but also a treat.

474
01:34:25,355 --> 01:34:26,996
[SPEAKER_01]: in terms of musical excellence.

475
01:34:27,496 --> 01:34:30,317
[SPEAKER_01]: She's bringing a wonderful group to you.

476
01:34:30,377 --> 01:34:33,879
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the Mina Cho Quartet, and it includes Dr. Cho.

477
01:34:33,919 --> 01:34:37,201
[SPEAKER_01]: It also includes George Lernes on drums.

478
01:34:40,562 --> 01:34:43,944
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, now here's where I could get messed up really, really bad.

