489
01:35:13,685 --> 01:35:15,866
[SPEAKER_01]: Ladies and gentlemen, the Minacho Quartet.

490
01:35:24,625 --> 01:35:25,445
[SPEAKER_00]: Hello, everyone.

491
01:35:25,525 --> 01:35:30,246
[SPEAKER_00]: Thank you so much for coming to this opportunity.

492
01:35:30,566 --> 01:35:36,188
[SPEAKER_00]: We are so grateful, and thank you so much, Terry and Jonathan, for your warm invitation.

493
01:35:36,568 --> 01:35:40,989
[SPEAKER_00]: The first tune we are playing is called G Street Dance.

494
01:35:41,229 --> 01:35:50,991
[SPEAKER_00]: I came up with this title, this cool title, and it is based on Korean traditional rhythm called gutgeori jangdan.

495
01:35:51,551 --> 01:35:54,232
[SPEAKER_00]: Geori means street, gut.

496
01:35:55,332 --> 01:35:58,475
[SPEAKER_00]: It has many meanings.

497
01:35:58,835 --> 01:36:06,380
[SPEAKER_00]: One of the meanings is shamanic ritual, but it can also be good performances or good rhythms.

498
01:36:07,180 --> 01:36:08,761
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess we are doing all of these.

499
01:36:09,222 --> 01:36:11,463
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a good performances, good rhythms.

500
01:36:11,483 --> 01:36:17,267
[SPEAKER_00]: We are prepared to play for you and it's a celebration for all of you, for the community.

501
01:36:17,367 --> 01:36:18,188
[SPEAKER_00]: Thank you so much.

