531
01:58:06,184 --> 01:58:09,446
[SPEAKER_00]: The next tune we are playing is called Dalmaji.

532
01:58:09,606 --> 01:58:10,047
[SPEAKER_00]: Guess what?

533
01:58:10,087 --> 01:58:12,429
[SPEAKER_00]: We have a lot of Korean titles today.

534
01:58:12,529 --> 01:58:16,212
[SPEAKER_00]: Dalmaji means greeting the moon.

535
01:58:16,432 --> 01:58:29,823
[SPEAKER_00]: In Korea, there's, in many Asian countries, as a matter of fact, there's a tradition of celebrating the night of the full moon, wishing for a happy year or rich harvest in the old days.

536
01:58:30,483 --> 01:58:41,954
[SPEAKER_00]: So this is my hope and our wish through this music you have a rich, I guess, emotions and good feelings and positive energy today.

537
01:58:42,755 --> 01:58:49,221
[SPEAKER_00]: So this is Dalmaji, Greeting the Moon, but I titled it Night of the Full Moon.

538
01:58:49,541 --> 01:58:50,402
[SPEAKER_00]: Night of the Full Moon.

