[SPEAKER_01]: In any case, Minichow on piano and Korean traditional instrument.

581
02:31:12,662 --> 02:31:20,144
[SPEAKER_01]: George Lennox on the drums, Young Taejong on bass, and Matthew Ryu on guitar.

582
02:31:25,565 --> 02:31:29,125
[SPEAKER_01]: Really, really different, beautiful music, obviously.

583
02:31:29,385 --> 02:31:34,947
[SPEAKER_01]: And really a change of pace from what we heard earlier in the day and what we heard yesterday.

584
02:31:36,347 --> 02:31:41,208
[SPEAKER_01]: And tomorrow, you'll want to be on hand if you can be.

585
02:31:42,248 --> 02:31:45,810
[SPEAKER_01]: We have the Niko Guerrero Trio.

586
02:31:46,510 --> 02:31:56,054
[SPEAKER_01]: We have another group from, as we have every year, from the Berklee Institute of Jazz and Gender Justice, which is directed by Terry Lynn Carrington.

587
02:31:56,634 --> 02:32:03,858
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, not to pat ourselves on the back, but myself, Jonathan Fagan back there,

588
02:32:05,987 --> 02:32:14,514
[SPEAKER_01]: Greg Toro and Gordon Engelgauld, the Ally Project, will be entertaining as the last set of the day.

589
02:32:14,594 --> 02:32:18,717
[SPEAKER_01]: So we hope that you can come back and enjoy the show.

590
02:32:19,618 --> 02:32:21,019
[SPEAKER_01]: It's been a blast.

591
02:32:21,039 --> 02:32:23,060
[SPEAKER_01]: A couple things I want to remind you of.

592
02:32:24,361 --> 02:32:28,725
[SPEAKER_01]: My friends, Tracy and Deakin from the Danish Pastry House.

593
02:32:32,506 --> 02:32:41,508
[SPEAKER_01]: They still have snacks available if you want some, you know, go inside and go inside and eat, yes, and enjoy.

594
02:32:42,408 --> 02:32:50,550
[SPEAKER_01]: And we've had just a wonderful, wonderful sponsorship from Method Community Media, my goodness.

595
02:32:52,670 --> 02:32:54,191
[SPEAKER_01]: Jim's here representing them.

596
02:32:55,871 --> 02:32:59,392
[SPEAKER_01]: We have audience, Avey Fagan is here.

597
02:33:00,688 --> 02:33:12,775
[SPEAKER_01]: Audience Sound Company, the Berklee Institute of Jazz for Gender Justice, Winchester Music School, Morningside Music Studio, the Arts Alive Foundation, and the Medford Arts Council.

598
02:33:13,935 --> 02:33:14,496
[SPEAKER_01]: It's been

599
02:33:16,058 --> 02:33:31,928
[SPEAKER_01]: a real special time for us, especially in terms of bringing on new Patreon subscribers who have helped to advance our efforts throughout the year, and then the sponsors that have jumped on board kind of towards the end of this thing.

600
02:33:33,189 --> 02:33:34,270
[SPEAKER_01]: Tomorrow, come on out.

601
02:33:35,211 --> 02:33:36,052
[SPEAKER_01]: We'll be here.

602
02:33:36,072 --> 02:33:38,133
[SPEAKER_01]: We'll be enjoying the day with you.

603
02:33:38,794 --> 02:33:40,175
[SPEAKER_01]: The tents will still be up.

604
02:33:40,416 --> 02:33:41,697
[SPEAKER_01]: The chairs will be here.

605
02:33:42,077 --> 02:33:43,418
[SPEAKER_01]: The music will be good.

606
02:33:43,999 --> 02:33:47,642
[SPEAKER_01]: And the food will still be available from Danish Pastry House.

607
02:33:48,463 --> 02:33:50,565
[SPEAKER_01]: Starts at 2 o'clock.

608
02:33:50,645 --> 02:33:55,649
[SPEAKER_01]: First band, Nico Guerrero Trio, Berklee Institute of Gender and Jazz.

609
02:33:58,006 --> 02:34:02,675
[SPEAKER_01]: Jazz and Gender Justice at three o'clock, and then the Ally Project at four o'clock.

610
02:34:03,496 --> 02:34:05,660
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you can go out for dinner after that, see?

611
02:34:06,538 --> 02:34:09,641
[SPEAKER_01]: You'll have had your fill of music and go out and get something nice to eat.

612
02:34:10,562 --> 02:34:12,383
[SPEAKER_01]: And you'll have made a day of it, right?

613
02:34:12,463 --> 02:34:16,787
[SPEAKER_01]: And then if you want to start with church, I'm not mad at you, OK?

614
02:34:17,448 --> 02:34:22,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Go get your worship on at the church, at the temple, wherever you serve.

615
02:34:22,152 --> 02:34:23,153
[SPEAKER_01]: Go on and do that.

616
02:34:24,153 --> 02:34:25,635
[SPEAKER_01]: In any case, thank you, Mina.

617
02:34:25,795 --> 02:34:26,756
[SPEAKER_01]: We appreciate you.

618
02:34:26,776 --> 02:34:28,117
[SPEAKER_01]: Appreciate you, fellas.

619
02:34:31,274 --> 02:34:32,595
[SPEAKER_01]: Appreciate our audience.

620
02:34:32,815 --> 02:34:34,877
[SPEAKER_01]: OK, so I said it before.

621
02:34:34,917 --> 02:34:36,198
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll say it one more time, right?

622
02:34:36,458 --> 02:34:37,859
[SPEAKER_01]: We're free, but we ain't cheap.

623
02:34:38,300 --> 02:34:43,444
[SPEAKER_01]: So if you want to make a donation, you can see my man Eli.

624
02:34:43,484 --> 02:34:45,105
[SPEAKER_01]: He's got the red box back there.

625
02:34:45,245 --> 02:34:47,547
[SPEAKER_01]: And he'll be happy to take your folding money.

626
02:34:51,631 --> 02:34:53,012
[SPEAKER_01]: Jonathan, did I forget anything?

627
02:34:53,773 --> 02:34:54,694
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, all right.

628
02:34:55,434 --> 02:34:58,717
[SPEAKER_01]: Show up tomorrow, okay?

629
02:34:58,897 --> 02:35:02,119
[SPEAKER_01]: And bring cash to donate, okay?

630
02:35:02,940 --> 02:35:06,462
[SPEAKER_01]: And eat, drink, and be merry, all right?

631
02:35:06,623 --> 02:35:09,385
[SPEAKER_01]: For tomorrow we live happy, all right?

632
02:35:09,705 --> 02:35:10,906
[SPEAKER_01]: Have a good evening, everybody.

633
02:35:10,946 --> 02:35:14,689
[SPEAKER_01]: Thank you for joining us here at the Medford Jazz Festival.

